Description: Port from MCP SDK 1.x to 2.0.0
 Upstream pins mcp[cli]<2, but Debian's python3-mcp is packaged at 2.0.0
 (no 1.x version available). SDK 2.0 renamed the API surface used here:
 .
  * mcp.server.fastmcp.FastMCP -> mcp.server.mcpserver.MCPServer, whose
    constructor now takes version= directly (the private _mcp_server
    attribute this code used to set the version on is gone).
  * The private low-level Server handle moved from server._mcp_server to
    server._lowlevel_server (same .run()/.create_initialization_options()
    API, just renamed).
  * mcp.types.JSONRPCMessage is now a plain Union type alias, not a
    pydantic model with .model_validate_json(); use the module-level
    mcp.types.jsonrpc_message_adapter (a pydantic TypeAdapter) instead.
  * mcp.types.Tool fields are now snake_case (input_schema/output_schema,
    serialized under their camelCase aliases on the wire).
  * The HTTP/SSE transports: FastMCP 1.x mcp.settings.{host,port,
    transport_security} is gone; pass them to run() instead.
 .
 Verified against python3-mcp 1:2.0.0-1.30~trixie: a real MCP ClientSession
 completes initialize() and tools/list() through the patched build (stdio),
 and the Streamable HTTP transport answers initialize on /mcp.
Author: Vítězslav Dvořák <info@vitexsoftware.cz>
Forwarded: not-needed
Last-Update: 2026-10-16

